# Line-ending policy.
#
# Gate G6 compares compiled output against a committed golden observation, and the
# golden asserts its own bytes (LF, trailing newline) so the diff a reviewer reads is
# the same on every platform. Git's autocrlf would rewrite those endings on a Windows
# checkout and the gate would fail on a correct tree — so the corpus and the golden are
# pinned to LF here rather than left to each contributor's git configuration.
tests/fixtures/determinism/**/*.md text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/determinism/golden.json text eol=lf

# Ingestion fixtures. The text ones are inputs to parsers that report line and
# byte positions, so their endings are pinned for the same reason the determinism
# corpus's are; the binary ones must never be touched by a line-ending filter at
# all, or the digest a test asserts changes on checkout rather than on edit.
tests/fixtures/ingest/*.md text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/ingest/*.html text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/ingest/*.rst text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/ingest/*.docx binary
tests/fixtures/ingest/*.pdf binary
tests/fixtures/ingest/inventory.json text eol=lf

# The inventory corpus (roadmap 4.7) sits one directory further down, and the
# element counts a gate asserts are counts of what a parser read: a line-ending
# filter rewriting a source on checkout would move them.
tests/fixtures/ingest/corpus/*.md text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/ingest/corpus/*.html text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/ingest/corpus/*.rst text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/ingest/corpus/*.docx binary
tests/fixtures/ingest/corpus/*.pdf binary
tests/fixtures/ingest/corpus/*.png binary

# The hostile suite is *all* binary, text-looking members included: a fixture is
# hostile because of its exact bytes — a nesting depth, a compression ratio, a
# truncation point — and a line-ending filter rewriting one on checkout would
# quietly weaken the test that guards against it (roadmap 4.2).
tests/fixtures/ingest/hostile/* binary

# The third judged corpus (roadmap 4.10). Its sources are the *inputs* the
# evidence was compiled from, and a judged anchor carries the source's digest in
# its filename — so a line-ending filter rewriting one on checkout would move
# every anchor that names it. The projected evidence is pinned to LF for the same
# reason the determinism corpus is: it is compared byte-for-byte against a fresh
# ingestion (`build_ingested_corpus.py --check`).
eval/corpora/uv-docs-ingested/sources/* binary
eval/corpora/uv-docs-ingested/sources/**/* binary
eval/corpora/uv-docs-ingested/knowledge/evidence/*.md text eol=lf
eval/corpora/uv-docs-ingested/eval/*.jsonl text eol=lf
eval/corpora/uv-docs-ingested/provenance.json text eol=lf
